{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us","id":344287,"title":"My Primary Problem With Wraith; or, \"Why do Asians have different souls than us?\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-18T18:19:18-08:00","id":344287,"title":"My Primary Problem With Wraith; or, \"Why do Asians have different souls than us?\"","content":"I believe the Deadguy has explained the reason behind the various Dark Kingdoms having different soul structures for the wraiths who die within them is based in cultural identifiers in the world of the living, which is fairly shaky logic but makes some degree of sense, especially in the context of consensual reality that the oWoD partially operates off of. Where that falls apart is that the Psyche/Shadow structure is a creation of the Wraith writing team with no particular significance in Western Europe and the United States, while everywhere else in the world has unique set-ups apparently based in their living counterparts (nevermind the fact that Africa and Asia are somehow monolithic enough to have one soul type cover their massively diverse populations).<br /> <br /> My question is then this; why is the Psyche/Shadow structure not universal? And failing that, why isn't the West characterized by something with clearer parallels in the thinking of the living?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T19:04:03-08:00","id":344308,"title":"","content":"The Psyche/Shadow structure is pretty universal. Terminology varies of course (Hun/P'o in the Yellow Springs) and some localized cosmological differences effect them differently, but that does seem to be bedrock soul-cosmology beneath local paradigmatic effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T16:26:03-08:00","id":345221,"title":"","content":"It's not a Wraith-centric issue at all.<br /> The CWoD as a whole was a victim of the 90's fascination with all things Asian.<br /> Through many game lines we were presented with characters from the East that from a Western perspective were &quot;similar to you but BETTER than you.&quot;<br /> In retrospect it's not only annoying for both sides but sometimes a little bit racist.<br /> But it was the 90's and stuff happened.<br /> It had very little to do with the actual writers and their beliefs. it was simply a sign of the times.<br /> I have a feeling a lot of this will be addressed as Onyx Path venture further into the 21st century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T23:58:22-08:00","id":345498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=345221#post345221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a Wraith-centric issue at all.<br /> The CWoD as a whole was a victim of the 90's fascination with all things Asian.<br /> Through many game lines we were presented with characters from the East that from a Western perspective were &quot;similar to you but BETTER than you.&quot;<br /> In retrospect it's not only annoying for both sides but sometimes a little bit racist.<br /> But it was the 90's and stuff happened.<br /> It had very little to do with the actual writers and their beliefs. it was simply a sign of the times.<br /> I have a feeling a lot of this will be addressed as Onyx Path venture further into the 21st century.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that some the of &quot;The Asian counterparts of X are different&quot; trend in the cWoD also just came out of an enthusiasm to write more material. It's fun and interesting to say &quot;how might this manifest differently?&quot;. Grabbing a geographic region and saying &quot;it's different here&quot; gives a writers lots of freedom to create more cool stuff; stuff that might not have fit well in the existing setting, but that still feels related to the core game. Some of the folks at WW might have initially siezed upon Asia for this because it was the 90s. After it had been done once in the WoD, there was a precedent set, so for later books it might have been seen as an established way to write exciting new setting variants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T08:24:19-08:00","id":345781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=345498#post345498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that some the of &quot;The Asian counterparts of X are different&quot; trend in the cWoD also just came out of an enthusiasm to write more material. It's fun and interesting to say &quot;how might this manifest differently?&quot;. Grabbing a geographic region and saying &quot;it's different here&quot; gives a writers lots of freedom to create more cool stuff; stuff that might not have fit well in the existing setting, but that still feels related to the core game. Some of the folks at WW might have initially siezed upon Asia for this because it was the 90s. After it had been done once in the WoD, there was a precedent set, so for later books it might have been seen as an established way to write exciting new setting variants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite all of them. Werewolf in the Beast Courts is very much like Werewolf in other parts of the world, just with more cooperation between various Changing Breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T08:58:30-08:00","id":345793,"title":"","content":"Something to consider. Castigate is the only Stygian Arcanoi NOT practiced in the Dark Kingdom of Jade. How do the wraiths of the Yellow Springs protect themselves during Maelstroms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T01:45:03-08:00","id":347259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Old Rusty Pipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=345793#post345793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to consider. Castigate is the only Stygian Arcanoi NOT practiced in the Dark Kingdom of Jade. How do the wraiths of the Yellow Springs protect themselves during Maelstroms?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Way of the Soul for dealing with yourself. Way of the Farmer dealing with Spectres.<br /> <br /> I know that Castigate is the only one canonically they're missing. I'm inclined though to throw in the Forbidden 3 though (maybe harvesting a few Mnemosyne powers for alternative Scholar powers) - and actually doesn't Merchant cover the Usury base pretty well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T03:35:09-08:00","id":347308,"title":"","content":"I would expand the list of Arcanoi they are forbidden to purchase as well. Not having Castigate is a bit of a hindrance though. The basic ability Bulwark protects against Maelstroms. The next Art that protects against such things would be Argos 2 (Storm Robes). I take this to mean that your average Yellow Springs wraith is going to be less mobile than your average Stygian wraith during a Maelstrom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3138-old-rusty-pipe","name":"Old Rusty Pipe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T05:03:01-08:00","id":347324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Old Rusty Pipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=347308#post347308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would expand the list of Arcanoi they are forbidden to purchase as well. Not having Castigate is a bit of a hindrance though. The basic ability Bulwark protects against Maelstroms. The next Art that protects against such things would be Argos 2 (Storm Robes). I take this to mean that your average Yellow Springs wraith is going to be less mobile than your average Stygian wraith during a Maelstrom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your &quot;average&quot; Stygian Wraith doesn't necessarily have any Castigate though. There are 13 different commonly available Stygian Arcanoi, so it's not like most Wraiths are optimized across the board.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T07:49:57-08:00","id":347408,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that most of the Great Maelstroms were never all that serious for the Yellow Springs, probably because most of them were caused by events in Europe and North America so it does make a bit of sense that the Jade wraiths would have less Maelstrom defenses as they haven't seen them as many of them. Plus as others have pointed out they have their own Arts for dealing with Angst and the Shadow.<br /> <br /> So not having Castigate does make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T11:20:29-08:00","id":347534,"title":"","content":"Which of course begs the question of why not? It's not like they weren't in an insidious decay of their own; insidious and inevitable decay is one of the key features of the underworld. Either the other Dark Kingdoms contributed to or at least experienced the Great Maelstroms, or they caused and experienced Maelstrom's of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T11:23:39-08:00","id":347536,"title":"","content":"Something else to remember, especially when discussing the Yellow Springs and Stygia, is that powerful beings mandated how things must be for the restless dead of wide swaths of the mortal world. Qin Shi Huangdi and Charon, respectively, had the power in the crazy days of yore to lay down laws for the dead, and these laws wound up with far more reach than only one nation or one specific group of 'former-mortals' (to coin a term). I mean, that's a very in-game view, but still...<br /> <br /> On another note, I choose to believe that all sorts of heretical pockets may exist in the extant Dark Kingdoms, possibly even extending as far as to allow for differing soul structures. These beliefs are likely localised and shared across the Veil, making it possible for something like, say, the Dark Kingdom of Obsidian to still exist in a very small capacity. Know, however, that I base this on some wonky, sometimes outside proper <b>Wraith</b> 'canon' sources (e.g. <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b>, <b>Exalted: the Abyssals</b>). That said, the World of Darkness is built on the premise that more options remain possible than what we see in any printed books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T11:37:10-08:00","id":347564,"title":"","content":"...Of course, the above does NOTHING to address the wonkiness of Sub-Saharan Africa's Dark Kingdom of Dark Darkness, or whatever they called it.<b>*</b> While I do like the idea of it, I've never been satisfied with the presentation of the Bush of Ghosts. That goes double for <i>Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom</i>, though the inclusion of Mla Watu was kind of fabulous, even if it came out in a dreadfully predictable fashion.<br /> <br /> <b>*</b> I DO know what it's called, by the bye. So no need to tell old knackered <b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Phaolan</span></b> what we all know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T11:48:35-08:00","id":347567,"title":"","content":"Forgive the clueless question but after reading Dark Kingdom of Jade and Kindred of the East, I don't see where we can say Asian people have different souls. The H'un/Po Psyche/Shadow is only a matter of semantics. Arcanoi being different can be chalked to cultural differences and the fact the Jade Emperor is heavily implied to be a Neverborn in disguise.<br /> <br /> So what is the &quot;differences&quot; between Asian Souls and others (except Far Shores beings, pardon me Yama Kings, being more active)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T17:58:06-08:00","id":347885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=347408#post347408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that most of the Great Maelstroms were never all that serious for the Yellow Springs, probably because most of them were caused by events in Europe and North America so it does make a bit of sense that the Jade wraiths would have less Maelstrom defenses as they haven't seen them as many of them. Plus as others have pointed out they have their own Arts for dealing with Angst and the Shadow.<br /> <br /> So not having Castigate does make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume the FIFTH was at least as bad in East Asia - I mean the nuking of two Japanese cities was the final trigger for it (after last decade of war and genocide).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T21:46:39-08:00","id":347990,"title":"","content":"Indeed. And that's one of the many reasons why the Yellow Springs are so keen to conquer Stygia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T18:58:25-08:00","id":358702,"title":"","content":"Im a bit scared... that Kuei-jin will be demoted to &quot;Random Cosmic accident&quot;<br /> <br /> I HATE that as an idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T20:48:52-08:00","id":358782,"title":"","content":"You mean the origin of the Kuei-Jin? They have a pretty full and complete origin that is most certainly <i>not</i> something random. They'd have to do a major retcon to make it a 'Random Cosmic accident'. That doesn't really strike me as something OPP would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T01:40:44-08:00","id":358921,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, the only wraith-like creatures <i>not</i> to have the Psyche/Shadow division (regardless of what you call it) are mummies. And the mummies aren't exactly &quot;naturally&quot; occurring - even by supernatural standards. It takes ritual magic performed by a(n awakened) mage to create a mummy, so that explains any differences right there.<br /> <br /> (For those who don't have <i>Mummy</i>, a mummy's soul splinters upon death. The &quot;ka&quot; has full access to both Skinlands and Shadowlands, but can't leave the body. The &quot;ba&quot;, meanwhile enters the Sunless Sea (Tempest/Dark Kingdom level), but can't enter the Shadowlands. . . until the body's repaired and ready to be reanimated. And the mummy's khabit (&quot;shadow&quot;) is completely suppressed the entire time (so no Shadowguiding or Harrowings. Or at least that's how it was - I don't have the last release)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=347534#post347534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of course begs the question of why not? It's not like they weren't in an insidious decay of their own; insidious and inevitable decay is one of the key features of the underworld. Either the other Dark Kingdoms contributed to or at least experienced the Great Maelstroms, or they caused and experienced Maelstrom's of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are official causes, recognized by the wraiths of Stygia. But who says they're right? If you want to have the &quot;real&quot; cause of a Great Maelstrom be something that happened elsewhere, go for it. Its not like wraiths (or the living) could easily communicate for most of history, so they couldn't exactly compare notes.<br /> <br /> From a writing standpoint, though, doing a true multi-cultural apocalypse is . . . complicated. Each culture has its own landmarks, values, social weak points . . . Finding something you can break in each culture to bring about an apocalypse, which will resonate with other cultures, is tough. If you're going for an epic feel, its much easier to pick a single culture, and run with it. Take a look at Susan Cooper's <b>Dark is Rising</b> quintet, or Clamp's <b>X</b>. From an outside perspective, it makes no sense why the fate of all humanity would rest with the British (Cooper), or the Japanese (Clamp). But from within the narrative, it works - and you don't end up with Japanese oni trying to invoke Celtic magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:00:10-08:00","id":360186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=347567#post347567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive the clueless question but after reading Dark Kingdom of Jade and Kindred of the East, I don't see where we can say Asian people have different souls. The H'un/Po Psyche/Shadow is only a matter of semantics. Arcanoi being different can be chalked to cultural differences and the fact the Jade Emperor is heavily implied to be a Neverborn in disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are mostly correct apart from the fact the Jade Emperor is in all likelihood an Onceborn in disguise, except one of the most ancient and powerful and millennia of wearing the Yu Huang mask made the two identities blur together to a degree.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-05-2015, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T10:37:28-08:00","id":360286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=360186#post360186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are mostly correct apart from the fact the Jade Emperor is in all likelihood an Onceborn in disguise, except one of the most ancient and powerful and millennia of wearing the Yu Huang mask made the two identities blur together to a degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes far more sense to me.<br /> It always struck me as odd. Yu Huang may be an irredeemable, sickening despot but he seems far more interesting in his own comfort than pulling the world down into Oblivion.<br /> If he was a Neverborn and was playing the long game, it is one hell of a looooooooong game.<br /> I like the idea that he/it doesn't really know what he is anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T11:21:30-08:00","id":360305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=347567#post347567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive the clueless question but after reading Dark Kingdom of Jade and Kindred of the East, I don't see where we can say Asian people have different souls. The <b>H'un/Po</b> Psyche/Shadow is only a matter of semantics. Arcanoi being different can be chalked to cultural differences and the fact the Jade Emperor is heavily implied to be a Neverborn in disguise.<br /> <br /> So what is the &quot;differences&quot; between Asian Souls and others (except Far Shores beings, pardon me Yama Kings, being more active)</div> </div> </div> </div>(Lengthy Linguistics Note Follows)<br /> <br /> Hun and P'o. Hun should not have an aspirant marker. P'o does, but English usually aspirates p to begin with, which is why Romanization of most Chinese languages moved away from adding in ' or h over the years to denote aspiration for initials. It's rather difficult to get most native English speakers to form an unaspirated t, p, or k, so use of d, b, and g, respectively, tended to replace them*, which is where you get Daoism instead of Taoism or Gong Fu instead of Kong Fu.<br /> <br /> *Such as Yale or Pinyin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T11:49:46-08:00","id":360389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/344287-my-primary-problem-with-wraith-or-why-do-asians-have-different-souls-than-us?p=360286#post360286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes far more sense to me.<br /> It always struck me as odd. Yu Huang may be an irredeemable, sickening despot but he seems far more interesting in his own comfort than pulling the world down into Oblivion.<br /> If he was a Neverborn and was playing the long game, it is one hell of a looooooooong game.<br /> I like the idea that he/it doesn't really know what he is anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so, although we also have another example (the city of Swar) of a Malfean (sort of) in disguise running a Dark Kingdom that seems much more interested in its own power, security, and comfort than in advancing the cause of Oblivion. I'd assume in both cases their peculiar origin and circumstances has given them a more complex personality than the average Onceborn. Moreover, DR:S and D:itL both suggested Onceborn are often just as invested in their own benefit as in fighting for Oblivion whereas the Neverborn are more mindful of the latter and Orpheus seems to indicate even the Neverborn's loyalty to Oblivion may have limits if their own survival is at stake.<br /> <br /> I think a good gauge may be the human parts of their personalities drive Lung Wang/Yu Huang and the city of Swar to care for their own comfort and security, and cause Yu Huang to show such quirks as an interest in ambitious infrastructure projects. In practical terms this becomes an interest to ensure the society of the Yellow Springs and Swar are built to stand in the long terms, are somewhat less instable and self-destructive than your average Amphiskiopolis, and can maintain a facade of being &quot;normal&quot; wraith societies. On the other hand, the Malphean parts of their personalities likely push them to make their Dark Kingdoms as brutal and oppressive for their own sake as they can get short of revealing their rulers' game. We also know of other examples of wraithly societies (e.g. several Far Shores) that came to be ruled by the Shadow-eaten and the same pattern tends to repeat.<br /> <br /> We know Charon may have been influenced by his Shadow at times during his career but he never became a Shadow-eaten. Things may be more ambigous with at least part of the Deathlords, at least a few may have fallen to their Shadows. It may be interesting to contrast and compare Stygia with the other major Dark Kingdoms and the one example of an Underworld society that is entirely from Oblivion's taint (the Ferrymen) to try and tell what in their bad aspects came from &quot;normal&quot; corruption of absolute power or good intentions gone bad and what was the influence of Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}